#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map to quantum problem {#step-1-map-to-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Hakbang 1: Map sa quantum problem {#step-1-map-to-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "1a: Setting up our Hamiltonian {#1a-setting-up-our-hamiltonian}"
msgstr ""
"1a: Pagse-set up ng ating Hamiltonian {#1a-setting-up-our-hamiltonian}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We use the Ising model on a line of 10 sites:\n"
msgstr "Ginagamit natin ang Ising model sa isang linya ng 10 site:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}_{\\text{Ising}} = \\sum_{i=1}^{9} J_{i,(i+1)} Z_i Z_{(i+1)} + \\sum_{i=1}^{10} h_i X_i \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}_{\\text{Ising}} = \\sum_{i=1}^{9} J_{i,(i+1)} Z_i Z_{(i+1)} + \\sum_{i=1}^{10} h_i X_i \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $J$ is the coupling strength between two sites and $h$ is the external magnetic field.\n"
"The [qiskit_addon_utils](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-utils/) package provides some reusable functionalities for various purposes.\n"
msgstr ""
"kung saan ang $J$ ay ang coupling strength sa pagitan ng dalawang site at ang $h$ ay ang panlabas na magnetic field.\n"
"Ang [qiskit_addon_utils](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-utils/) package ay nagbibigay ng ilang reusable na functionalities para sa iba't ibang layunin.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Its [qiskit_addon_utils.problem_generators](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-utils/stubs/qiskit_addon_utils.problem_generators.html) module provides functions to generate Heisenberg-like Hamiltonians on a given connectivity graph.\n"
"This graph can be either a [rustworkx.PyGraph](https://www.rustworkx.org/apiref/rustworkx.PyGraph.html) or a [CouplingMap](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.CouplingMap) making it easy to use in Qiskit-centric workflows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang [qiskit_addon_utils.problem_generators](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-utils/stubs/qiskit_addon_utils.problem_generators.html) module nito ay nagbibigay ng mga function para bumuo ng mga Heisenberg-like Hamiltonian sa ibinigay na connectivity graph.\n"
"Ang graph na ito ay maaaring [rustworkx.PyGraph](https://www.rustworkx.org/apiref/rustworkx.PyGraph.html) o [CouplingMap](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.CouplingMap) na ginagawang madaling gamitin sa mga Qiskit-centric workflow.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the following, we create a simple line of 10 qubits using the "
"`CouplingMap.from_line` method.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa mga sumusunod, gumagawa tayo ng simpleng linya ng 10 qubits gamit ang "
"`CouplingMap.from_line` method.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "![Code output](/img/qiskit-addons/mpf/01-getting-started/output_1.png)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Code output](/img/qiskit-addons/mpf/01-getting-started/output_1.png)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, we generate the "
"[SparsePauliOp](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp)"
" on the provided connectivity with the desired constants.\n"
msgstr ""
"Susunod, bumubuo tayo ng "
"[SparsePauliOp](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp)"
" sa ibinigay na connectivity gamit ang nais na mga constant.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The observable that we will be measuring is the total magnetization which we"
" can simply construct as shown below:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang observable na susukatin natin ay ang kabuuang magnetization na maaari "
"nating buuin nang simple tulad ng ipinapakita sa ibaba:\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "1b: Multi-Product Formulas {#1b-multi-product-formulas}"
msgstr "1b: Multi-Product Formulas {#1b-multi-product-formulas}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"MPFs reduce the Trotter error of Hamiltonian dynamics through a weighted "
"combination of several circuit executions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Binabawasan ng mga MPF ang Trotter error ng Hamiltonian dynamics sa "
"pamamagitan ng weighted combination ng ilang circuit execution.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "To make this more concrete, we define an MPF as:\n"
msgstr "Para gawing mas konkreto ito, tinutukoy natin ang isang MPF bilang:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mu(t) = \\sum_{j} x_j \\rho^{k_j}_{j}\\left(\\frac{t}{k_j}\\right) + \\text{some remaining Trotter error} \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mu(t) = \\sum_{j} x_j \\rho^{k_j}_{j}\\left(\\frac{t}{k_j}\\right) + \\text{some remaining Trotter error} \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $x_j$ are our weighting coefficients, $\\rho^{k_j}_j$ is the density "
"matrix corresponding to the pure state obtained by evolving the initial "
"state with the product formula, $S^{k_j}$, involving $k_j$ Trotter steps, "
"and $j$ indexes the number of product formulas that make up the MPF.\n"
msgstr ""
"kung saan ang $x_j$ ay ang ating weighting coefficients, ang $\\rho^{k_j}_j$"
" ay ang density matrix na tumutugma sa pure state na nakuha sa pamamagitan "
"ng pag-evolve ng inisyal na state gamit ang product formula, $S^{k_j}$, na "
"may kasamang $k_j$ Trotter steps, at ang $j$ ay nag-iindex sa bilang ng mga "
"product formula na bumubuo sa MPF.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The key here is that the remaining Trotter error is smaller than the Trotter"
" error that one would obtain by simply using the largest $k_j$ value!\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang susi dito ay ang natitirang Trotter error ay mas maliit kaysa sa Trotter"
" error na makukuha sa pamamagitan ng simpleng paggamit ng pinakamalaking "
"$k_j$ value!\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "You can view the usefulness of MPF from two perspectives:\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari mong tingnan ang pagiging kapaki-pakinabang ng MPF mula sa dalawang "
"perspektibo:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For a fixed budget of Trotter steps that you are able to execute, you can "
"obtain results with a Trotter error that is smaller in total.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa fixed na badyet ng mga Trotter step na maaari mong isagawa, "
"makakakuha ka ng mga resulta na may mas maliit na Trotter error sa "
"kabuuan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For a number of Trotter steps which results in deep circuits, you can use "
"MPF to find several shorter-depth circuits to run which result in a similar "
"Trotter error.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa isang bilang ng mga Trotter step na nagreresulta sa malalim na mga "
"circuit, maaari mong gamitin ang MPF upang makahanap ng ilang mas maikling-"
"depth na mga circuit na patatakbuhin na nagreresulta sa katulad na Trotter "
"error.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "An introduction to static MPFs {#an-introduction-to-static-mpfs}"
msgstr "Isang panimula sa mga static na MPF {#an-introduction-to-static-mpfs}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"_Static_ MPFs are those where the $x_j$ values do **NOT** depend on the "
"evolution time, $t$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga _static_ na MPF ay yaong ang mga $x_j$ value ay **HINDI** "
"nakadepende sa evolution time, $t$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Determining the static MPF coefficients for a given set of $k_j$ values amounts to solving a linear system of equations:\n"
"$Ax=b$, where $x$ are our coefficients of interest, $A$ is a matrix depending on $k_j$ and the type of PF we use ($S$), and $b$ is a vector of constraints.\n"
"For brevity, we are not going to go into more detail here and instead refer you to the documentation of [LSE](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mpf/apidocs/qiskit_addon_mpf.costs.html#qiskit_addon_mpf.costs.LSE).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pagtukoy ng static MPF coefficients para sa ibinigay na set ng mga $k_j$ value ay nangangahulugan ng paglutas ng linear system of equations:\n"
"$Ax=b$, kung saan ang $x$ ay ang ating mga coefficient na interesado, ang $A$ ay isang matrix na nakadepende sa $k_j$ at sa uri ng PF na ginagamit natin ($S$), at ang $b$ ay isang vector ng mga constraint.\n"
"Para sa kaiklian, hindi tayo magpapakadetalyado pa dito at sa halip ay isasangguni ka natin sa documentation ng [LSE](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mpf/apidocs/qiskit_addon_mpf.costs.html#qiskit_addon_mpf.costs.LSE).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can find a solution for $x$ analytically as $x = A^{-1}b$, see e.g. [Carrera Vazquez et al., 2023] or [Zhuk et al., 2023].\n"
"However, this exact solution can be _\"ill-conditioned\"_ resulting in very large L1-norms of our coefficients, $x$, which can lead to bad performance of the MPF.\n"
"Instead, one can also obtain an approximate solution which minimizes the L1-norm of $x$ in order to attempt and optimize the MPF behavior.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari nating mahanap ang solusyon para sa $x$ nang analytical bilang $x = A^{-1}b$, tingnan hal. [Carrera Vazquez et al., 2023] o [Zhuk et al., 2023].\n"
"Gayunpaman, ang exact na solusyon na ito ay maaaring _\"ill-conditioned\"_ na nagreresulta sa napakalaking L1-norms ng ating mga coefficient, $x$, na maaaring humantong sa masamang performance ng MPF.\n"
"Sa halip, maaari ring makakuha ng approximate na solusyon na nag-mi-minimize ng L1-norm ng $x$ upang subukang i-optimize ang gawi ng MPF.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In the following, you will learn how to do all of this.\n"
msgstr "Sa mga sumusunod, matututuhan mo kung paano gawin ang lahat ng ito.\n"

#. type: Link reference
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Carrera Vazquez et al., 2023]: https://quantum-"
"journal.org/papers/q-2023-07-25-1067/"
msgstr ""
"[Carrera Vazquez et al., 2023]: https://quantum-"
"journal.org/papers/q-2023-07-25-1067/"

#. type: Link reference
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Zhuk et al., 2023]: "
"https://journals.aps.org/prresearch/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevResearch.6.033309"
msgstr ""
"[Zhuk et al., 2023]: "
"https://journals.aps.org/prresearch/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevResearch.6.033309"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Choosing $k_j$ {#choosing-k-j}"
msgstr "Pagpili ng $k_j$ {#choosing-k-j}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The choice of $k_j$ is up to the end-user.\n"
"In principle, any values can be chosen but some $k_j$'s will lead to a larger noise amplification on real devices than other choices.\n"
"Thus, it is important that one tries to find _\"good\"_ values of $k_j$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pagpili ng $k_j$ ay nasa end-user.\n"
"Sa prinsipyo, anumang halaga ang maaaring piliin ngunit ang ilang $k_j$ ay hahantong sa mas malaking noise amplification sa mga totoong device kaysa sa ibang mga pagpili.\n"
"Kaya, mahalagang subukan ng isa na maghanap ng _\"magagandang\"_ value ng $k_j$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, we will simply pick some fixed values for $k_j$.\n"
"The smallest value is motivated by the target evolution time of $t=8.0$ which normally tells us to satisfy $t/k_{\\text{min}} \\lt 1$ but empirically we know that setting it equal to $1$ usually works, too.\n"
"If you want to learn more about this and how to choose your other $k_j$ values, refer to the respective guide: [How to choose the Trotter steps for an MPF](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mpf/how_tos/choose_trotter_steps.html).\n"
msgstr ""
"Dito, kukunin lang natin ang ilang fixed na value para sa $k_j$.\n"
"Ang pinakamaliit na value ay binigyang-katwiran ng target evolution time na $t=8.0$ na karaniwang nagsasabi sa atin na masiyahan sa $t/k_{\\text{min}} \\lt 1$ ngunit empirikal na alam natin na ang pagtatakda nito sa katumbas ng $1$ ay karaniwang gumagana rin.\n"
"Kung gusto mong matuto pa tungkol dito at kung paano pumili ng iba pang $k_j$ value, sumangguni sa kaukulang guide: [How to choose the Trotter steps for an MPF](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mpf/how_tos/choose_trotter_steps.html).\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Setting up the LSE {#setting-up-the-lse}"
msgstr "Pagse-set up ng LSE {#setting-up-the-lse}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now that we have chosen our $k_j$s, we must first construct the LSE, $Ax=b$ as explained above.\n"
"The matrix $A$ depends not only on $k_j$ but also our choice of product formula (PF) -- in particular its _order_.\n"
"Additionally, one may take into account whether the PF is symmetric or not (see [Carrera Vazquez et al., 2023]), by setting `symmetric=True`.\n"
"However, this is not required as shown by [Zhuk et al., 2023].\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon na napili na natin ang ating mga $k_j$, dapat muna nating buuin ang LSE, $Ax=b$ tulad ng ipinaliwanag sa itaas.\n"
"Ang matrix na $A$ ay nakadepende hindi lamang sa $k_j$ kundi pati na rin sa ating pagpili ng product formula (PF) -- partikular ang _order_ nito.\n"
"Bukod pa rito, maaaring isaalang-alang ng isa kung ang PF ay symmetric o hindi (tingnan ang [Carrera Vazquez et al., 2023]), sa pamamagitan ng pagtatakda ng `symmetric=True`.\n"
"Gayunpaman, hindi ito kinakailangan tulad ng ipinakita ng [Zhuk et al., 2023].\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, we are going to use a second-order Suzuki-Trotter formula yielding "
"`order=2` and we will set `symmetric=True`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dito, gagamit tayo ng second-order Suzuki-Trotter formula na nag-yi-yield ng"
" `order=2` at itatakda natin ang `symmetric=True`.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Solving for $x$ analytically {#solving-for-x-analytically}"
msgstr "Paglutas para sa $x$ nang analytical {#solving-for-x-analytically}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "As mentioned before, we can find $x$ analytically:\n"
msgstr ""
"Tulad ng nabanggit dati, maaari nating mahanap ang $x$ nang analytical:\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Optimizing for $x$ using an exact model {#optimizing-for-x-using-an-exact-"
"model}"
msgstr ""
"Pag-optimize para sa $x$ gamit ang exact model {#optimizing-for-x-using-an-"
"exact-model}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alternatively to computing $x=A^{-1}b$, you can also use "
"[setup_exact_problem](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-"
"mpf/stubs/qiskit_addon_mpf.costs.setup_exact_problem.html) to construct a "
"[cvxpy.Problem](https://www.cvxpy.org/api_reference/cvxpy.problems.html#cvxpy.Problem)"
" instance which uses the LSE as constraints and whose optimal solution will "
"yield $x$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bilang alternatibo sa pagkalkula ng $x=A^{-1}b$, maaari mo ring gamitin ang "
"[setup_exact_problem](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-"
"mpf/stubs/qiskit_addon_mpf.costs.setup_exact_problem.html) upang bumuo ng "
"[cvxpy.Problem](https://www.cvxpy.org/api_reference/cvxpy.problems.html#cvxpy.Problem)"
" instance na gumagamit ng LSE bilang mga constraint at ang optimal na "
"solusyon nito ay magbibigay ng $x$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In the next section, it will be clear why this interface exists.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa susunod na seksyon, magiging malinaw kung bakit umiiral ang interface na "
"ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As an indicator whether an MPF constructed with these coefficients will "
"yield good results, we can use the L1-norm (see also [Carrera Vazquez et "
"al., 2023]).\n"
msgstr ""
"Bilang indikasyon kung ang isang MPF na binuo sa mga coefficient na ito ay "
"magbibigay ng magagandang resulta, maaari nating gamitin ang L1-norm "
"(tingnan din ang [Carrera Vazquez et al., 2023]).\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Optimizing for $x$ using an approximate model {#optimizing-for-x-using-an-"
"approximate-model}"
msgstr ""
"Pag-optimize para sa $x$ gamit ang approximate model {#optimizing-for-x-"
"using-an-approximate-model}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It may happen that the L1 norm for the chosen set of $k_j$ values is deemed too high.\n"
"If that is the case and you cannot choose a different set of $k_j$ values, you can use an approximate solution to the LSE instead of an exact one.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaaring mangyari na ang L1 norm para sa napiling set ng mga $k_j$ value ay tinuturing na masyadong mataas.\n"
"Kung ganoon ang kaso at hindi ka makakapili ng ibang set ng mga $k_j$ value, maaari kang gumamit ng approximate na solusyon sa LSE sa halip na exact.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To do so, simply use "
"[setup_sum_of_squares_problem](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-"
"mpf/stubs/qiskit_addon_mpf.costs.setup_sum_of_squares_problem.html) to "
"construct a different "
"[cvxpy.Problem](https://www.cvxpy.org/api_reference/cvxpy.problems.html#cvxpy.Problem)"
" instance which constrains the L1-norm to a chosen threshold while "
"minimizing the difference of $Ax$ and $b$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para gawin ito, gamitin lang ang "
"[setup_sum_of_squares_problem](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-"
"mpf/stubs/qiskit_addon_mpf.costs.setup_sum_of_squares_problem.html) upang "
"bumuo ng ibang "
"[cvxpy.Problem](https://www.cvxpy.org/api_reference/cvxpy.problems.html#cvxpy.Problem)"
" instance na nagpapaliit sa L1-norm sa napiling threshold habang minimi-"
"minimize ang pagkakaiba ng $Ax$ at $b$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note, that you have complete freedom over how to solve this optimization problem, meaning that you can change the optimization solver, its convergence thresholds, and so on.\n"
"Check out the respective guide on [How to use the approximate model](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mpf/how_tos/using_approximate_model.html).\n"
msgstr ""
"Tandaan, na mayroon kang ganap na kalayaan kung paano malulutas ang optimization problem na ito, ibig sabihin maaari mong baguhin ang optimization solver, ang convergence thresholds nito, at iba pa.\n"
"Tingnan ang kaukulang guide sa [How to use the approximate model](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mpf/how_tos/using_approximate_model.html).\n"

